---
description: How to apply SEO head tags from Populr without creating duplicates or breaking JSX
alwaysApply: false
---

When applying SEO changes from Populr (`get_seo_fixes`, `get_structured_data`):

- One `<title>` and one `<meta name="description">` per page. Replace existing ones; never add a second.
- Prefer the framework's metadata API (Next.js `metadata` / `generateMetadata`, Nuxt `useHead`, Remix `meta`, `<svelte:head>`) over hand-written tags.
- JSON-LD: one block per `@type`. Replace an existing block of the same type. In JSX, render it with `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` and escape `<` as `<`.
- Apply only what Populr returns as approved. Suggest other changes through `draft_page_fix`, which the owner approves in Populr.
